WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.750
Am I going to die?

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:11.130
You already have.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.700
Who are you?

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.020
Inga.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:43.410
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:50.000
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:55.420
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:58.840
Things never get any better.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.760
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:09.060
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:14.530
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:20.280
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:26.410
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:32.170
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.130
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:38.470
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:44.060
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:50.560
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.940
I really wanna call this off.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.530
Don't say that. This is a party for the Kanou group!

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:03.380
It's such a pain to have to wear a 19th-century party dress.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.540
This skirt's like <i>this</i>, and the corset's like <i>this</i>!

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:07.260
You're very well read...

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:07.810
I sure am-

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.690
...in manga.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:09.670
Well...

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.930
There's no need to worry.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.800
Since it's a costume party, President Kanou sent this dress for you.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.440
The design is rather plain, though.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.370
Geez, you're too forceful.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.680
With this, you won't need to feel
embarrassed as the Master's representative.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.970
His representative?!

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.060
That President Kanou... They were saying on TV
that he's going to be arrested today or tomorrow.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.480
They say whatever they want on TV.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.720
Anyway...

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:41.710
I am not at all okay with going to that party alone.

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.400
Ah, that looks great on you, Rie.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.680
Father!

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.820
It must have been a pain to put on.

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.030
Back then,

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.340
in order to encourage equal trade relations with foreign countries,

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.870
a party was held in the Rokumeikan.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:08.170
Kanou is intending this as an opportunity to
start anew in forging international relations.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:10.200
I appreciate you taking care of my role.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.640
Wait a sec-

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.400
Master, Koyama-san of the Public Prosecutor's Office...

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.650
Izumi-san?

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.190
President Kaishou.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.830
If you don't show your face at Kanou's party today-

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:20.520
Excuse me-

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:22.610
Kanou-san is my friend.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.620
As an outside advisor to us prosecutors, you can infiltrate this party.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.100
Excuse me-

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:30.500
This is a chance for you to ask him questions directly-

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:37.090
I have accepted the role of acting as Kaishou Rinroku's representative this evening.

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:39.340
You're just trying to cause trouble.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.640
This elevator is reserved; you'll have to take a different one!

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.640
We're lucky. There's plenty of room!

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.050
I wanna push it!

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:50.840
Hit the top floor.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:51.560
Got it!

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.440
You two...

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.430
What business do you have at tonight's party?

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.360
An invitation?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.790
Doesn't look like you were the one who sent these out.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.740
Of course not, why would I-

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.720
Um, Koyama-san. Who are these people?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.490
Don't mind them. They'll dirty your clothes if you get any closer.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:11.370
Huh?! I'm clean, Izumi-chan!

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.830
Don't act so friendly with me.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.170
This is President Kaishou's-

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.540
You're Rinroku's daughter, huh?

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.530
How dare you call the President by name!

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:24.590
Nowadays, the only thing an owner of a shady net
business does is monopolise money and technology...

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:27.480
...and act as an advisor to every ministry and agency.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.080
What the heck?

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.640
You dressed as Napoleon too, Kanda-san?

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.390
My wife said there's no alternative.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.770
So international banks are prospering even now.

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.450
That's not so!

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.780
I owe everything to you.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:44.030
That said, how is Kanou-san's...

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:45.990
The prosecution...

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:49.870
The newly appointed Joint Coordinating
Dept. intend to arrest him no matter what.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.640
If that happens, we too will-

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.890
Kanou-san, thank you for inviting me toni-

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:03.890
Kanou-kun!

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.090
The police would have to be running wild to think of arresting you!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.600
At tonight's party, I'll dispel all suspicion of you!

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.350
I'm sorry to cause you both so much trouble.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.540
As his wife, you must be having a hard time, too.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.350
It's too bad that there was no choice but to host it in your own home.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.330
I'm just too afraid to leave here.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.360
Well then, shall we?

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.110
I've come as Kaishou Rinroku's representative.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.640
My name is Rie.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:32.810
Thank you so much for coming.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.030
Thank you kindly.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:35.490
Kaishou-sensei's-

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.580
Well, well,

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:40.190
I've never had the chance to meet with Kaishou-san,

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.460
but allow me to introduce myself!

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.300
So Kaishou-sensei actually exists...

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:46.800
The chairman is here?

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:47.780
Chairman Kaishou!

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.660
Kaishou-san!

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.620
Is he here?!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.430
Sensei!

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.430
Stay back!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.650
It's fine.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.430
Nice to meet you, everyone.

00:05:59.430 --> 00:06:00.900
If you're here at the party,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.470
it means that Chairman Kaishou supports President Kanou,

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.900
and that he trusts in his innocence.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.400
Ah, that's right.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.030
Hey, hey, President Kanou!

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:15.830
Thank you so much for inviting me tonight.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:18.710
W-Who are you?

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:20.320
This very individual...

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:22.850
...shines light upon a world gripped with desire...

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.880
...and is known to the people as The Last Great Detective,

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.760
Yuuki Shinjuurou!

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.300
Yuuki? It feels like I've heard that name somewhere.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:35.180
He's the one who always shows up at crime scenes
and criticises President Kaishou's brilliant deductions!

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:38.890
Ah, I remember the newspapers
calling him "The Defeated Detective".

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.190
So why are you here?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.190
Who knows?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:46.820
But the fact that I was called here
means that a crime is going to occur.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.190
A major crime.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:52.030
First they go after Kanou, then they
try to get close to Chairman Kaishou.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:53.200
They have no honour.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.570
Pardon me, Milady!

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.450
That's Yuuki Shinjuurou?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.460
The Defeated Detective.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.350
There is no one who loves his country more than Kanou Nobuzane!

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:07.590
These recent accusations are nothing more than the
state bending to the complaints of foreign countries.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:11.220
Kanou-kun, I will give it my all to defend you!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:16.300
Thank you.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.770
Moving along, I would like to hear a word from Kanda Masahiko...

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.020
...of the Japanese International Currency Bank.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:23.020
Ono passes on reconstruction work to Kanou,

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.400
and Kanda lends financial aid to foreign countries.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.900
But amidst this triangle, there's money disappearing.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.900
Good evening to you all. Next, President Kanou will-

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:36.160
What do you people want?

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.780
Mr. Detective isn't with you?

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:43.420
You can't possibly think you were helping me out with that stunt back there.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.370
I hate that "Defeated Detective"!

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.670
Is there a room above this one?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:50.750
President Kanou's home consists of this one floor.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.340
How did you know?

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:54.260
Who are you?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:56.930
Milady.

00:07:58.690 --> 00:08:02.310
There was no need to go through the trouble of having an SP guard me.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.230
SP?

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.360
If anything were to happen to Milady, it would be a disaster.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:09.150
My regards.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:13.900
Come, let us toast.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.120
What might you be toasting to?

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:22.830
That the charges brought on by you
prosecutors will be dismissed, of course.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:25.950
Milady!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:27.560
Are you all right?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:28.460
I'm sorry.

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:32.570
The alcohol must have gone right to your head.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.100
Milady, how do you feel?

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:48.640
I'm fine now, Madam.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:09:05.370
At this time, I, Kanou Nobuzane, have something I want to say to everyone concerning the suspicions raised against me.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:08.320
Is he trying to claim innocence before the entire crowd?

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.380
What terrible taste.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:26.520
Madam?

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.150
I seems that something has happened!

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:37.410
I'm Hayami of the Metropolitan Police.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.530
An investigation squad will arrive shortly, so do not dist-

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:43.980
The Joint Coordinating Dept. is allowed the right to our own investigation.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.680
The criminal is within this hall.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:48.290
We need to search for the person who killed Kanou Nobuzane-

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.420
Rather than "who", the real question may be "why".

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.300
Darling!

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:00.890
Representative Kanda, Congressman Ono!

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:02.940
What do you want?

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:06.520
Where were the two of you when the lights went out?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.560
What are you saying all of a sudden?

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.150
Are you trying to imitate Chairman Kaishou?

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.820
"The man who's lead so many cases to a resolution"-

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:19.400
Before the lights went out, there was someone in a Napoleon outfit close to the stage.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.480
Many others have corroborated this.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.920
Which of us are you saying is the culprit, then?

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:25.260
Perhaps even both of you.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.200
What?!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:32.300
Kanou-san has been suspected of embezzling the support funds of foreign countries,

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.960
and both Ono-sensei and Kanda-san were involved in this.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:37.420
If Kanou-san had been arrested,

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:39.160
you would both be in a bit of trouble.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:40.380
That's ridiculous!

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:43.790
When the lights went out, I was talking with Kanda-kun.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.620
I can also guarantee Ono-sensei's innocence!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:50.100
You two strategically chose a costume that would stand out,

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.980
expecting that you could ensure one another's alibi.

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:57.650
Yes.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.240
Understood.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:04.990
Mr. Defeated Detective.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.240
There won't be a need for you.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.760
Your father also likes to play something close to a detective, but...

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.190
My father is nothing like you!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:18.130
He merely offers advice for the sake of this country's future!

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.220
Sorry, Rie.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.340
Could you move aside for a bit?

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:30.090
Everyone, this is Chairman Kaishou.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.970
I'm Kaishou Rinroku.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:35.720
I was a friend of Kanou-san.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:39.190
I won't be able to come to the scene, but I can offer my opinion.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.850
The wisdom of Chairman Kaishou has
contributed to the solving of innumerable cases.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:45.450
He is a special advisor to the Joint Coordinating Dept.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:48.900
Father! The culprits are Ono-sensei and Representative Kanda!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.200
That's not possible.

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.430
Father?!

00:11:51.430 --> 00:11:56.170
They are wearing the same outfit, but they stand out far too much.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:02.840
But there hasn't been any mention of
other suspicious people near the stage.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.720
Oh, but they were there.

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:11.100
They were certainly there, but they soon
escaped the hold of everyone's consciousness.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.060
They're still there, in fact.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:17.940
I see... the SP.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.320
The security guards!

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:25.240
These days, whenever a gathering is held with important people, there are security guards and SP deployed there.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.740
But since they're expected, no one pays attention to them.

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:30.490
You're saying that an SP murdered Kanou?

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.510
I see... That's what happened.

00:12:33.510 --> 00:12:34.120
Madam?

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:38.000
Kanou... My husband wasn't stealing support funds at all!

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:44.260
He was asked to conceal some of the funds by a government official.

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:48.010
He intended to reveal this tonight.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.780
But prior to that, some dog of the government went and-

00:12:50.780 --> 00:12:52.020
That's ridiculous!

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:02.530
The residents' elevator...

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:07.350
She pretended to leave the hall along with us, then turned right back,

00:13:07.350 --> 00:13:09.660
and when the lights went out, she...

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:12.290
She would have been informed about the evening's schedule as well.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.420
This is too cruel! How could you...

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:16.060
You're mistaken, Madam!

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.420
Just how am I mistaken?

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.420
Shinjuurou...

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:20.540
I'm at my limit.

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:22.800
Be patient.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:27.610
Inga!

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:29.350
The police... yes, the police...

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:32.060
No, even higher than that.

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:34.200
You paired up with them to kill Kanou, didn't you?!

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.120
That's not true!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.060
Yes it is!

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.800
It isn't true.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.690
It most definitely isn't.

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.980
Why is only her coat removed?

00:13:45.030 --> 00:13:51.210
If the police or the prosecutors had used this woman to assassinate Kanou Nobuzane...

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.370
Which they certainly did!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:55.210
...why is she dead?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.500
This is quite a luxurious space for just the two of you.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:04.430
If the police are suspected of assassinating Kanou,

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:07.210
then it invalidates the suspicion that an SP was the culprit.

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:09.860
That's why you're saying suicide is out of the question, right?

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:14.430
But if she was intending revenge on Kanou, it's
possible that she may have killed herself afterwards.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.490
If that were the case, she could have just shot him out in the open.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:19.220
Why a knife?

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:19.940
Well...

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:28.360
With these, anyone with a dark suit would look like an SP.

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.530
Someone impersonated an SP?

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:36.430
Without a doubt, the person in question
had control over when the lights went out.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:39.040
They caught the female SP off guard,

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:41.160
shot her to death, impersonated her,

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.480
and headed back to the hall.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.890
She then approached Mr. Kanou naturally.

00:14:49.190 --> 00:14:52.590
There were only two people who were outside the hall at that time.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.370
I-It wasn't me!

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.180
Mrs. Kanou...?

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.040
Don't say things like that.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.880
My husband was just murdered!

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.890
How could you suspect me?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:05.940
What reason would I have to kill him?

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:10.740
Yes, I too would love to hear your reason.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:13.450
Another one.

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.200
Who the heck is that?

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:18.630
She's my... boss, I suppose.

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.960
My name is Inga, little princess.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:26.220
Answer me just one thing.

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.210
What?

00:15:28.830 --> 00:15:30.450
Well...

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:34.510
Got it!

00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:41.980
All right now.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:45.990
Tell me,

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:49.230
was your husband a criminal in your eyes?

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.550
The man you loved?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.710
Or... what?

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:56.830
There's no purpose in me answering that.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.700
Tell me.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:09.840
Tell me.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:13.220
What was your husband to you?

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.220
What?

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.400
What?

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:35.530
A hero.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:42.960
He had no choice but to be a hero.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.530
What... just happened?

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:47.520
She can ask one question,

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:50.210
which people have no choice but to answer.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:52.790
What do you mean by a hero?

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:54.590
Have you already forgotten?

00:16:56.120 --> 00:17:01.470
Until recently, we were at war.

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:10.500
In response to our full-scale troop deployment,

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.270
terrorist groups launched multiple attacks against us.

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:16.280
I know. There was a war,

00:17:16.280 --> 00:17:17.880
but it's over now.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.620
It's merely in an unsettled state.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:26.250
During the war, Kanou dedicated funding to
fighting terror in this country and was praised for it!

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:27.750
But after the war,

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.510
all anyone would say was that he was stealing it for himself!

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:32.880
Even though the victims of terrorism are treated as heroes...

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:38.640
Even though those of us who survived
are just trying to get on with our lives...

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:43.350
I couldn't allow that man, who lived for his country, to be arrested.

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:44.520
He...

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.420
He had to die as a hero!

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:58.660
That's why you stabbed him,

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.890
after killing the SP and impersonating her.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.430
But what about evidence?

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.210
The SP's jacket had been taken off.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:13.460
It's likely that she borrowed the jacket from the SP before she returned to the hall.

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:16.830
She then failed to put it back on the SP.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.290
But the bottom half...

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.470
I hear that that kind of dress can be changed into and out of quickly.

00:18:23.470 --> 00:18:24.140
Yes.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:29.200
Then under all that fluff, you'd be able to wear pants, wouldn't you?

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.080
They're probably on even now.

00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:35.320
Those shoes...

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:47.700
If the police had killed him, Kanou wouldn't have been a criminal,

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.850
he would have been the victim of government conspiracy.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.850
You went so far as to kill an innocent SP for that purpose?

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:55.380
More people than that died in the war, didn't they?

00:18:57.130 --> 00:19:01.980
During the war, we secured supplies
from all over the world for this country,

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:05.260
and now, when we earn money, it's evil?

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:07.880
The war is at fault!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:11.520
It's because of the war that we're falling apart.

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:12.400
It's too much.

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:16.230
Humans fall to corruption.

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:18.450
So too do saints and heroes.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.930
There's no stopping it.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.110
That in itself is salvation.

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:27.620
Phone call. It's for you.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.890
It seems that you were just a step ahead of me yet again.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:35.660
Are you sure you didn't know from the very beginning?

00:19:35.660 --> 00:19:41.380
But unfortunately, as usual, the female SP is going to be presented as the criminal.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:48.400
That's it: "Kanou's wife noticed this and
shot the SP before the police could do it."!

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:49.890
I wonder if that's a good enough story.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:55.830
"Kanou-san's embezzlement of goods was a false charge, someone's conspiracy"!

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:57.860
That keeps his honour intact as well.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:00.010
A beautiful outcome, huh?

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.400
I hope it suits your fancy.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:18.210
Huh? Where did that woman go?

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:19.480
Huh? Ah...

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.800
She said she was tired and went home.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:23.110
I see.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:27.020
Um... I'm sorry!

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.930
I hadn't known.

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.600
My father's reasoning was off the mark the whole time,

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:33.960
and you've been the one who was right.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.280
But my father and Koyama-san never let that...

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:42.790
I always lose. I'm the "Defeated Detective" after all.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:48.100
But I'm sure his wife really believed that Kanou-san was a hero.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:52.370
A hero who fought hard to protect his family and company amidst this chaotic world.

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:56.100
Such a beautiful lie must exist...

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:57.710
...um...

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:03.840
To end something beautiful in a beautiful way, huh?

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:05.840
Yes.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.170
That's not something we can really relate to,

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.350
since we're constantly in the process of falling.

00:21:30.490 --> 00:21:38.540
Wandering hazily on a pale morning, hearing a whispered prayer,

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:46.510
You and I trace a twisted scenery.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:54.180
We're seeking the (truth). "We don't even care if it's a lie."

00:21:54.640 --> 00:21:58.560
As if we can see right through it,

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:02.520
We follow it along.

00:22:02.520 --> 00:22:06.490
Looking for, going beyond words,

00:22:06.570 --> 00:22:10.490
Like a falling feather.

00:22:10.490 --> 00:22:13.620
Looking for, find it,

00:22:14.490 --> 00:22:19.960
So we can come closer together.

00:22:34.470 --> 00:22:38.480
Looking for, unravel it,

00:22:38.480 --> 00:22:42.480
Tear it apart, like a cloud.

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:45.570
Looking for, find it,

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:50.410
So we can come closer together.

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:59.120
I hear that the next episode is based on Sakaguchi Ango's 「Meiji-era Ango Detective Stories "Les Misérables"」.

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:00.750
Let's give it a read.

00:23:01.100 --> 00:23:04.130
Um, what's a "sketchy rickshaw man"?

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:05.090
"Pourboire"?

00:23:05.090 --> 00:23:06.990
An "English Twist"?

00:23:06.990 --> 00:23:08.260
Wait a second, Shinjurou!

00:23:08.260 --> 00:23:10.710
This story is completely different!

00:23:10.710 --> 00:23:12.110
It's saying the bad guy is xxxxx,

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:14.260
but we haven't had an xxxxx show up at all!

00:23:15.140 --> 00:23:16.700
UN-GO, Episode 2:

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:17.680
Heartless Song!

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:19.930
Wait, what's a "gilly"?!
